  <section class="syl-first-week">
    <h2>Start here: your first module</h2>
    <p>This is an eight-week course. It moves fast, and Module 1 is the setup
    module for everything after it. Do these five things in the first week.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Take the Syllabus Quiz</strong> in Blackboard. It is untimed,
        you get multiple attempts, and it is worth 6 points.</li>
      <li><strong>Post to the Introduction Discussion</strong> (10 points, the
        largest single item in Module 1).</li>
      <li><strong>Install the stack</strong>: VS Code, R, and GitHub Copilot for
        Students, authenticated, by the end of Module 1. There is a setup
        walkthrough screencast and a confirmation submission. Module 5 cannot be
        done on a phone or tablet.</li>
      <li><strong>Pick your primary AI tool</strong> and a second one for
        cross-checking, and file the AI Tool Inventory.</li>
      <li><strong>Start your AI Use Log.</strong> It runs through every module
        and it is the spine of this course, not an add-on.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Read the <a href="#ai-use-policy">AI Use Policy</a> before you submit
    anything. This course overrides SIUE's default prohibition: AI use here is
    <strong>required</strong>, and undisclosed AI use is still academic
    dishonesty.</p>
