  <h2 id="how-to-reach-me">How to reach me</h2>

  <p>The communication model in this course is built around <strong>weekly
  office hours</strong>. Those are the canonical channel for instructor-student
  support.</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Office hours (synchronous, weekly)</strong> are the primary
      support channel. In person Tuesday and Thursday from 12:30 to 1:45 PM and
      3:30 to 5:00 PM in 1017 Dunham Hall (drop-in, no appointment needed), or remotely
      by appointment through <a href={BOOKINGS}>Microsoft Bookings</a>, which
      shows you only my open times. Office hours are never recorded, so you can
      speak freely about grades, accommodations, or anything else.</li>
    <li><strong>Email</strong>
      (<a href="mailto:aleith@siue.edu">aleith@siue.edu</a>) is for formal
      requests, time-non-sensitive questions, and confidential issues (grades,
      accommodations). Expect a response within 24 hours on weekdays.</li>
    <li><strong>Course discussion forums (Blackboard)</strong> are the place for
      student-to-student discussion. I participate periodically but do not
      monitor continuously; bring instructor-directed questions to office hours
      or email.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>There is no Discord channel for this section. The course's communication
  architecture is intentionally narrow so the channels that exist work well.</p>

  <p>In all communication, clearly stated needs save us both time. State what
  you have tried, what is not working, and what kind of response you are hoping
  for.</p>

