  opportunities to address mistakes for partial credit are provided.</p>

  <p><strong>Quizzes are untimed.</strong> The Syllabus Quiz and any Blackboard
  quizzes in this course are untimed, and you may take multiple attempts. If any
  timed element is ever added, it will be announced in advance with
  ACCESS-coordinated lead time so that accommodations can be arranged.</p>

  <p><strong>Feedback timeline.</strong> Grades with feedback are posted by the
  Friday following the due date for formative assignments, and within 7 days for
  summative assignments. Final Pitch Deck feedback arrives within 48 hours of
  the due date, since final grades are due shortly after. Find your grades under
  <strong>My Grades</strong> in the Blackboard course menu.</p>

  <p><strong>Late work.</strong> Assignments are due before or on the date
  specified. Late assignments lose 10% per business day for up to one week.
  After one week, the assignment receives a zero unless an accommodation has
  been arranged in writing before the original due date. An eight-week course
  does not have the schedule flexibility of a sixteen-week course. If you are
  experiencing an emergency, contact me as early as possible; I work with
  students case by case when contacted proactively, but I cannot extend
  deadlines retroactively.</p>

  <p><strong>Rewrites.</strong> Formative assignments (type F) may be revised and
  resubmitted within one week of grade posting for full credit. Summative
  assignments (type S) with rubric scores below 70% may be revised and
  resubmitted within one week; the final grade for a resubmission is averaged
  between the original and the revised submission.</p>

